Privacy Policy for Assetora

Last updated: September 17, 2026

This Privacy Policy explains how Assetora (“Assetora,” “we,” “us,” or “our”) handles information when you use the Assetora mobile application (the “App”). By using the App, you acknowledge this Policy.

1. Information We Collect and Process
Account and authentication information
You may browse much of the App without an account. An account is required to download assets and to use account-based features such as likes, saved assets, and comments. When you create an account with email and password, we process your display name, email address, Firebase user ID, and authentication information. Passwords are submitted to Firebase Authentication; Assetora does not store your plaintext password in its Firestore user record.

If you choose Sign in with Google, Google and Firebase Authentication provide the information needed to authenticate you, such as your email address, Firebase user ID, and basic profile information made available by your Google account. We do not receive your Google password.

Account activity and content
For signed-in users, we store and sync your saved assets, liked asset IDs, viewed asset IDs, and the related asset metadata needed to show your library. If you post a comment, we store the comment text, your Firebase user ID, display name, the asset ID, timestamps, and whether the comment was edited. We also maintain aggregate view and like counts for assets.

Local app data and device information
The App stores the following on your device using local app storage: a randomly generated Assetora device identifier, the IDs of assets you have viewed, app settings (theme, autoplay, and skip preference), temporary navigation/cache data, and a background timestamp. This release does not transmit the locally generated device identifier to our server and does not use it as the identifier for likes or views. The local viewed-assets list helps prevent repeat view-count increments on the same app installation; when you are signed in, that list is also synced to your account.

Technical information processed by service providers
Firebase Authentication may process information such as IP address and user-agent data to authenticate users, secure sign-in, and prevent abuse. Network providers involved in delivering the App’s web-based interface, icons, media, or Firebase services may also receive standard connection information such as your IP address and request metadata.

Notifications and downloads
If you allow notifications, the App may show device notifications about new assets or administrator updates. The App does not request location, contacts, camera, microphone, or phone-number access in this release. When you download an asset, its URL and title are passed to your device’s download feature or browser so the file can be saved on your device.

2. How We Use Information
We use the information described above to:

create, authenticate, and manage your account;
provide downloads, comments, likes, saved assets, viewing history, and synchronized account features;
maintain aggregate asset metrics and reduce duplicate view counting on an app installation;
display App content and notifications you choose to receive;
operate, secure, troubleshoot, and improve the App; and
comply with applicable legal obligations and enforce our terms.
3. Service Providers and Sharing
We use Google Firebase to provide Firebase Authentication and Cloud Firestore. Firebase Authentication manages sign-in, and Cloud Firestore stores the account and App-content data described in this Policy. Google acts as a service provider/processor for these services. You can read Google’s Firebase privacy and security information and Privacy Policy.

Google Sign-In is optional. If you select it, your use of Google Sign-In is also subject to Google’s policies. We do not sell personal information or use it for interest-based advertising. We share information only as described in this Policy, when required by law, to protect rights and safety, or as part of a merger, acquisition, or similar corporate transaction.

4. Data Retention
We retain account and App-activity data while your account is active and for as long as needed to provide the App, resolve disputes, meet legal obligations, or enforce our agreements. Data stored only on your device remains there until you clear the App’s storage or uninstall the App. Firebase’s processing and retention are governed by its applicable terms and privacy documentation.

5. Your Choices and Account Deletion
You may sign out at any time. You can manage local information by clearing the App’s storage or uninstalling the App. To request access to, correction of, or deletion of your Assetora account and associated Firestore data, email hexacrewdev@gmail.com from the email address linked to the account, with the subject line “Assetora Privacy Request.” For deletion requests, we will delete the Firebase Authentication account and associated account data, including saved assets, likes, viewed-asset history, and comments, unless we must retain limited information for a legal reason.

6. Security
We use reasonable safeguards designed to protect information, including the security controls provided by Firebase. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.

7. Children’s Privacy
Assetora is not designed for children under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child has provided us personal information, please contact us so that we can take appropriate action.

8. International Processing
Firebase services may process information in the United States and other countries where Google or its service providers operate. By using the App, you understand that your information may be processed in countries that may have privacy laws different from those in your country.

9. Changes to This Policy
We may update this Policy from time to time. We will post the updated version in the App or at the privacy-policy URL and revise the “Last updated” date. Your continued use of the App after an update means you acknowledge the updated Policy.

10. Contact Us
If you have questions, suggestions, or a privacy request, contact us at [hexacrewdev@gmail.com]
